    <guid>https://quartz.jzhao.xyz/topics/integration-by-substitution-(indefinite)</guid>
    <description><![CDATA[  Write out the integral \displaystyle{\int \dfrac{\ln x}{x(1+\ln x)^2}}\text{ d}x Change what you are integrating with respect to \displaystyle{\int \dfrac{\ln x}{x(1+\ln x)^2}}\dfrac{\text{ d}x}{\text{ d}u}\text{ d}u Use the substitution given to find the derivative; differentiate as is. ]]></description>
